 "test": "crates/engine/src/cmd/patterns_tests.rs: circular_pattern_of_spokes_tangent_to_a_hub_joins (PR #3612, paused)",
 "summary": "Five box spokes 72 degrees apart joined one after another to a hub (r 12) inside a ring (r 63..66), thickness 2 in a 3 mm body. With the spoke's inner face exactly on the hub cylinder (x = 12, line contact) SolidCraft's earlier kernel returned a volume about 355 mm3 too large at the 4th union. Volumes are closed form: ring + hub = 1593*pi = 5004.5571; a spoke adds 2*(2*F(63,1.25) - x0*2*1.25) with F(r,z) = (z*sqrt(r^2-z^2) + r^2*asin(z/r))/2, minus its sliver inside the hub when x0 < 12. Tolerances: 1 mm3 at the exact tangency (the bug was 355 mm3), 0.01 mm3 on the two controls, which differ from each other by 0.048 mm3 and are told apart by their lump count. At the exact tangency only the volume is checked: the contact is a line, so lump and face counts are not ground truth.",
